WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.890
A container port: steel
boxes stacked high,

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:05.730
cranes loading ships.

3
00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:12.950
World Bank figures put the world's goods
exports in 2024 at 24.62 trillion dollars.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.750
Now a call centre, or a data centre.

5
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.170
Nothing here is loaded onto a ship.

6
00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:23.830
World service exports that
year: 8.88 trillion dollars.

7
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.130
Much smaller.

8
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:28.470
So if goods still dominate,
why have services,

9
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.070
and trade among developing
countries, grown faster?

10
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.110
In this mission, you'll
sort trade into goods,

11
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.310
services and capital, and see
what the world's goods really are.

12
00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.590
Then you'll track the rise of trade
from one developing country to another.

13
00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:47.890
Your mission: explain why services,
and trade among developing countries,

14
00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.320
have grown faster.
